*  frame_alt_two_instances - TWO placed ARBNO instances EACH re-entered for its
*  second alternative.  altarg_red needs one re-entry; this needs per-instance
*  state at depth 2, i.e. the LIFO chain, not a single slot.
*  Oracle trace on 'abab': instance1 'a' fails onward, retry 'ab'; instance2 'a'
*  fails onward, retry 'ab'; RPOS(0) => MATCH.
        inner = ('a' | 'ab')
        outer = ARBNO(*inner)
        s = 'abab'
        s POS(0) *outer RPOS(0)                               :S(G)F(B)
G       OUTPUT = 'match'                                      :(END)
B       OUTPUT = 'nomatch'
END
